<td id="A1.T1.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T1.2.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Number of microbatches</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T1.2.14.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Number of hosts</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section derives analytic expressions for throughput and per-token delay in model-parallel LLM inference deployments. All symbols are defined in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix A Performance Modeling ‣ SiPipe: Bridging the CPU–GPU Utilization Gap for Efficient Pipeline-Parallel LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We first analyze a single-node configuration, where a single inference engine is partitioned across multiple GPUs using either tensor parallelism (TP) or pipeline parallelism (PP), and then extend the LLM to cross-node settings.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>Pure Tensor Parallelism</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each transformer layer performs two <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">allreduce</em> communication operations under TP. Including start-up latency, the communication cost on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs is</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{comm-TP}}(N)=2L\times(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>comm-TP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{comm-TP}}(N)=2L\times(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the overall throughput of the inference system is:</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b}{t_{\text{comp-TP}}(N)+t_{\text{comm-TP}}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>comp-TP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>comm-TP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b}{t_{\text{comp-TP}}(N)+t_{\text{comm-TP}}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L\alpha\log_{2}N+4sbhL/B_{1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L\alpha\log_{2}N+4sbhL/B_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Correspondingly, the per-token delay—the reciprocal of throughput—is:</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(N)=\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L\alpha\log_{2}N+4sbhL/B_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(N)=\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L\alpha\log_{2}N+4sbhL/B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Pure Pipeline Parallelism</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pipeline parallelism splits a batch of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> sequences into <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> microbatches , so each stage produces <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b/m</annotation></semantics></math> tokens per iteration.
For one stage the latency is:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stage}}=\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stage</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stage}}=\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence overall throughput is:</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{t_{\text{stage}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stage</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{t_{\text{stage}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E5Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A single token experiences <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> compute phases and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> inter-stage transfers, so its end-to-end delay is</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(N)=N\times\frac{L\,C}{N}+(N-1)\times sbh/B_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(N)=N\times\frac{L\,C}{N}+(N-1)\times sbh/B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Hybrid Model Parallelism</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In production, tensor and pipeline parallelism are often enabled together to fit larger models, so the system incurs communication overheads from each.
Let <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> be the tensor-parallel degree and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> the pipeline-parallel degree (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\times t=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\times t=N</annotation></semantics></math>).
Combining the two previous models yields:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}+\frac{2L}{p}(\alpha\log_{2}t+2sbh/B_{1})};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{1}+\frac{2L}{p}(\alpha\log_{2}t+2sbh/B_{1})};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(\frac{L\,C}{N}+\frac{2L}{p}(\alpha\log_{2}t+2sbh/B_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(\frac{L\,C}{N}+\frac{2L}{p}(\alpha\log_{2}t+2sbh/B_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(p-1)sbh/B_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(p-1)sbh/B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Multi-node Model Parallelism</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When an inference instance spans multiple nodes, part of the communication occurs over a slower inter-node network with bandwidth <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> hosts are connected through this network, then the performance of pure tensor parallelism is:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(N)=\frac{b}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(N)=\frac{b}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(N)=\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(N)=\frac{L\,C}{N}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For pure pipeline parallelism, only the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> inter-stage transfers that cross hosts use bandwidth <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; the remaining <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-n</annotation></semantics></math> transfers stay on the faster intra-node link <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L\,C+(n-1)sbh/B_{2}+(N-n)sbh/B_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L\,C+(n-1)sbh/B_{2}+(N-n)sbh/B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Put them together, the combined throughput and per-token delay are:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{2}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{b/m}{\frac{L\,C}{N}+sbh/B_{2}+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L\,C+(n-1)sbh/B_{2}+(N-n)sbh/B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L\,C+(n-1)sbh/B_{2}+(N-n)sbh/B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2L(\alpha\log_{2}N+2sbh/B_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">From the models above we note two insights:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Throughput scaling.</span> Pipeline parallelism scales almost linearly with the number of GPUs, whereas tensor parallelism hits a throughput ceiling: although computation is divided further, the communication volume stays constant (or even grows), so GPU utilization plateaus.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(2) <span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Latency trends.</span> Increasing the tensor-parallel degree quickly lowers per-token latency, while deeper pipeline parallelism lengthens it because each token must traverse more stages.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
